node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
docs/_wiki/

# The journal itself IS committed: it is the record that survives a machine, and a teammate reading it is
# the point. Only the stop marker is ignored — it is overwritten on every turn that moves HEAD, so tracking
# it would put a one-line diff in front of every commit and teach people to ignore the diff.
.atlas/last-stop

# The server's claim on a port, rewritten on every start — churn, not record.
.atlas/serve.pid
# Which session was last told the dashboard URL, so the line is said once per session rather than after
# every tool call. A session id, meaningful only on the machine that produced it.
.atlas/serve-announced
.atlas/artifact-page.html

# Generated launcher pages — rewritten by `atlas serve --launcher`, published as artifacts.
.atlas/atlas-dashboard.html
.atlas/dashboards.html
# Held for the length of a build, released after — churn, not record.
.atlas/build.lock

# Which build last built here, so a second one can say it disagrees. It names an absolute path on one
# machine, so committing it would put someone else's checkout location in everybody's diff.
.atlas/build.owner.json
